<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The posting queue's keybinding.

  Auto-loaded by the client, deliberately NOT listed in GoldCap.toc, which is how a
  Bindings.xml file is meant to be shipped.

  Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-17-post-queue-design.md, section "Keybinding".
  This does NOT call the button's own Click method: the wiki is explicit that a click made
  that way inherits the caller's taint and skips RegisterForClicks and the mouse-down
  handling. Instead it calls the exact same Lua function the posting queue's toolbar button
  calls from its own OnClick (see GC.Sell.Attach in UI/SellFrame.lua, which assigns
  f.GoldCapPostNext = onQueueClick). Bindings.xml executes as an isolated chunk with no
  upvalues into any addon file, so a reachable global is the only way in.

  A keybinding handler runs synchronously inside a real hardware input event, which is what a
  protected post actually requires. Whether the client's hwevent check is satisfied by THIS
  path specifically has not been confirmed in game.

  Note for whoever edits this comment next: XML forbids a double hyphen anywhere inside a
  comment. Writing one the way Lua starts a comment makes the whole file fail to parse with
  "not well-formed (invalid token)", the keybinding silently never registers, and the client
  throws a Lua Warning on load. spec/bindings_xml_spec.lua now fails the build for it.
-->
<Bindings>
  <Binding name="GOLDCAP_POST_NEXT" header="GOLDCAP">
    if GoldCapSniperFrame and GoldCapSniperFrame.GoldCapPostNext then
      GoldCapSniperFrame.GoldCapPostNext()
    end
  </Binding>
</Bindings>
